itize ex-ante standards and shared safety benchmarks over ex-post litigation that destroys small firms. I challenge you to explain how your trigger prevents a well-funded incumbent from using discovery-on-demand to bankroll a 'death by a thousand cuts' strategy against a superior, smaller competitor. Without a clear mechanism to shield nascent firms from the crippling costs of this discovery process, your policy will not produce safety; it will produce a stagnant, monopolized industry.",
